---
/**
 * Synchronous request path and the asynchronous outbox hand-off. Shows why a
 * commerce write answers before webhooks, email and plugin deliveries run.
 */
---

<figure class="fc-diagram">
  <svg
    class="fc-seq"
    viewBox="0 0 920 650"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="fc-sync-title fc-sync-desc"
  >
    <title id="fc-sync-title">Fastcart request and asynchronous outbox flow</title>
    <desc id="fc-sync-desc">
      An admin request enters the HTTP edge, resolves the store, runs the
      workflow, writes the module transaction and appends an outbox event in the
      same transaction, then returns 200. After the response, the dispatcher
      claims the event, fans it out per subscription, and delivers it to
      webhooks, email or plugins with retries.
    </desc>

    <defs>
      <marker
        id="fc-sync-arrow"
        viewBox="0 0 10 10"
        refX="9"
        refY="5"
        markerWidth="7"
        markerHeight="7"
        orient="auto-start-reverse"
      >
        <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" class="fc-arrow"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <rect class="fc-box-accent" x="5" y="24" width="110" height="36" rx="7"></rect>
    <text class="fc-label-strong" x="60" y="46" text-anchor="middle">Admin SPA</text>

    <rect class="fc-box-accent" x="145" y="24" width="110" height="36" rx="7"></rect>
    <text class="fc-label-strong" x="200" y="46" text-anchor="middle">HTTP edge</text>

    <rect class="fc-box" x="295" y="24" width="110" height="36" rx="7"></rect>
    <text class="fc-label-strong" x="350" y="46" text-anchor="middle">Store DB</text>

    <rect class="fc-box-brand" x="435" y="24" width="110" height="36" rx="7"></rect>
    <text class="fc-label-strong" x="490" y="46" text-anchor="middle">Workflows</text>

    <rect class="fc-box" x="565" y="24" width="110" height="36" rx="7"></rect>
    <text class="fc-label-strong" x="620" y="46" text-anchor="middle">Outbox + jobs</text>

    <rect class="fc-box" x="690" y="24" width="110" height="36" rx="7"></rect>
    <text class="fc-label-strong" x="745" y="46" text-anchor="middle">Dispatcher</text>

    <rect class="fc-box" x="805" y="24" width="110" height="36" rx="7"></rect>
    <text class="fc-label-strong" x="860" y="46" text-anchor="middle">Integrations</text>

    <path class="fc-lifeline" d="M 60 60 V 560"></path>
    <path class="fc-lifeline" d="M 200 60 V 560"></path>
    <path class="fc-lifeline" d="M 350 60 V 560"></path>
    <path class="fc-lifeline" d="M 490 60 V 560"></path>
    <path class="fc-lifeline" d="M 620 60 V 560"></path>
    <path class="fc-lifeline" d="M 745 60 V 560"></path>
    <path class="fc-lifeline" d="M 860 60 V 560"></path>

    <!-- Synchronous request -->
    <path class="fc-line" d="M 60 105 H 198" marker-end="url(#fc-sync-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="fc-mono-muted" x="66" y="99">PATCH /api/v1/admin/products</text>

    <path class="fc-line" d="M 200 135 h 30 v 12 h -30" marker-end="url(#fc-sync-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="236" y="129">request id · auth · CSRF</text>

    <path class="fc-line" d="M 200 165 H 348" marker-end="url(#fc-sync-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="206" y="159">open store pool</text>

    <path class="fc-line" d="M 200 195 H 488" marker-end="url(#fc-sync-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="206" y="189">mutate(product)</text>

    <path class="fc-line" d="M 490 225 H 352" marker-end="url(#fc-sync-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="484" y="219" text-anchor="end">transaction</text>

    <path class="fc-line-dashed" d="M 350 255 H 488" marker-end="url(#fc-sync-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="356" y="249">committed</text>

    <path class="fc-line" d="M 490 285 H 618" marker-end="url(#fc-sync-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="496" y="279">append event (same tx)</text>

    <path class="fc-line-dashed" d="M 200 315 H 62" marker-end="url(#fc-sync-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="194" y="309" text-anchor="end">200 OK</text>

    <!-- Async boundary -->
    <path class="fc-line-dashed" d="M 20 355 H 900"></path>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="460" y="372" text-anchor="middle">after the HTTP response · at-least-once</text>

    <path class="fc-line" d="M 745 405 H 622" marker-end="url(#fc-sync-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="739" y="399" text-anchor="end">claim due rows (2 s tick)</text>

    <path class="fc-line" d="M 745 435 h 30 v 12 h -30" marker-end="url(#fc-sync-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="781" y="429">fan out per subscription</text>

    <path class="fc-line" d="M 745 465 H 858" marker-end="url(#fc-sync-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="751" y="459">webhook · email · plugin</text>

    <path class="fc-line-dashed" d="M 860 495 H 747" marker-end="url(#fc-sync-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="854" y="489" text-anchor="end">2xx / retry</text>

    <path class="fc-line" d="M 745 525 H 622" marker-end="url(#fc-sync-arrow)"></path>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="739" y="519" text-anchor="end">done · backoff</text>

    <rect class="fc-tag" x="60" y="590" width="800" height="40" rx="7"></rect>
    <text class="fc-sub" x="74" y="610">
      The outbox row commits with the business write. Delivery happens after the response; five failed
      attempts move an event to the dead letter.
    </text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    <strong>Figure 2.</strong> The synchronous request path ends at the store
    transaction. Since webhooks, email and plugin deliveries run after commit,
    the merchant gets a fast response and integrations get durable retries.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
